{"name":"Winter Wedding","hex":"#f1e4dc","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Traditionally the fourth of the four seasons, typically regarded as spanning either the period between the winter solstice to the spring equinox, or the months of December, January, and February in temperate and polar regions of the Northern Hemisphere and the months of June, July, and August in the Southern Hemisphere. It is the time when the sun is lowest in the sky, resulting in short days, and the time of year with the lowest atmospheric temperatures for the region.","The period of decay, old age, death, or the like."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the winter (in a particular place).","To store something (for instance animals) somewhere over winter to protect it from cold."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winter"},{"term":"wedding","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A marriage ceremony; a ritual officially celebrating the beginning of a marriage.","The joining of two or more parts."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of wed"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wedding"}],"entries":[{"title":"Winter","blocks":[{"text":"Winter is the coldest and darkest season of the year in temperate and polar climates. It occurs after autumn and before spring, when the hemisphere is oriented away from the Sun as a result of the tilt of Earth's axis. Different cultures define different dates as the start of winter, and some use a definition based on weather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Winter_forest_silver.jpg/330px-Winter_forest_silver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter","wikidata":"Q1311"},{"title":"Wedding","blocks":[{"text":"A wedding is a ceremony in which two people are united in marriage. Wedding traditions and customs vary greatly between cultures, ethnicities, races, religions, denominations, countries, social classes, and sexual orientations. Most wedding ceremonies involve an exchange of marriage vows by a couple; a presentation of a gift ; and a public proclamation of marriage by an authority figure or celebrant. Special wedding garments are often worn, and the ceremony is sometimes followed by a wedding reception. Music, poetry, prayers, or readings from religious texts or literature are also commonly incorporated into the ceremony, as well as superstitious customs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Hindu_wedding_rituals_b_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Hindu_wedding_rituals_b_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedding","wikidata":"Q49836"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Winter_forest_silver.jpg/500px-Winter_forest_silver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Winter_forest_silver.jpg/1280px-Winter_forest_silver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Winter_forest_silver.jpg/500px-Winter_forest_silver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWinter_forest_silver.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Earth-satellite-seasons.gif/500px-Earth-satellite-seasons.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Earth-satellite-seasons.gif/500px-Earth-satellite-seasons.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Animation of snow cover changing with the seasons","link":"https://